  "text": "Back to app\nCtrl\n+\nF\n\nAI CAPABILITIES\n\nAgents\nAI Provider Accounts\nOPTIONAL\nOrchestration\nComputer Use\nVoice\n\nSET UP\n\nOrca Account\nGeneral\nIntegrations\nMobile\n\nWORKFLOWS\n\nAutomations\nArtifacts\nBETA\nShare Skills\nBETA\nAgent Session Search\nGit & Source Control\nTask Sources\nTerminal\nQuick Commands\nBrowser\nMobile Emulator\nFloating Workspace\n\nINTERFACE\n\nAppearance\nChat UI\nInput & Editing\nNotifications\nShortcuts\nStats & Usage\n\nREMOTE HOSTS\n\nSSH Hosts\nRemote Orca Servers\n\nPRIVACY & SECURITY\n\nPrivacy & Telemetry\n\nADVANCED\n\nAdvanced\n\nEXPERIMENTAL\n\nExperimental\nPlugins\nALPHA\n\nPROJECTS\n\nIndependent project\nSSH\nRemote Orca Servers\n\nRun Orca on another machine and work on it from here.\n\nAdd server\nShare this computer\n\nNew projects open on this computer until you add a server.\n\nNo saved servers\n\nPair a dev box, a cloud machine, or a desktop at home. Its sessions keep running there when this computer sleeps.\n\nConfigure usage tracking\nOff\n—\n·\n0\n0 hosts\nChat UI is here\nExplain login\nMap out how login works\nRead\nauth.ts\n\nLogin starts in auth.ts: the browser posts to /login, the server checks the password and creates a session, then redirects you to the app. Here’s the flow:\n\nBrowser\npassword\n/login\nSession\ncookie\nApp\nAsk anything, @ to mention files, / for commands\nAsk for approval\nOpus\nAgents can now open as a chat, with rich messages, visuals and images.\nChange anytime in Settings → Chat UI.\nStay in terminal\nUse Chat UI",
